  "reason": "For #228, the follow-up of the review of #225: DEC-116 says which manifests rust-item reads (the root's, else each directory at its top), that only a build script's output under the build directory is not compared, that a directory of the docs that cannot be listed whole is unread, and that docs where a crate held depends by a path on a crate of the project whose source pages they lack have no trace; V-145 names the new tests of the holding and of the kind of each unknown name; the shared helpers of the end-to-end tests gained the one fixture of the sources of hand-written docs, and the tests that wrote it by hand use it with no expected answer changed. Read against the code by its author; what each document claims still holds, by the tests it names, which are left to CI on the pull request",
